abstract: >-
  Tests that a HANK code must pass at limits with known answers or at exact identities (permanent-income
  household-block limit, TANK benchmark with imposed incidence, Werning (2015) vanishing liquidity,
  Aiyagari no-idiosyncratic-risk limit, intertemporal Keynesian cross consistency, HANK - RANK differencing
  identity), reported as errors and observed convergence orders rather than single pass/fail checks. Version 0.3.0
  adds checks V1-V6 computed from primitive quantities the code reports (GE target residual of the vanishing-liquidity
  solve, steady-state market-clearing and budget residuals, income normalisation, the documented specification along
  equilibrium paths, and the solved exogenous paths against the requested ones), with a verdict that missing or
  non-finite values cannot hide, and mutation tests of the suite on hand-made and independently generated errors.
  A numerical audit before the release found no negative mass in the stationary solver and no effect of its
  absolute value or weight clip on the results; it led to one change, a fixed backward-iteration seed in the
  permanent-income calibration.
  Reference implementation on sequence-jacobian 1.0.0, with minimal reproductions of three observations about that
  library (F1, F2, F3). Developed with extensive assistance
  from Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic) and reviewed with GPT 6.1 Sol (OpenAI); the author directed and reviewed
  the work and is responsible for the content. See the AI usage disclosure in the README.
keywords:
  - HANK
  - heterogeneous agents
  - sequence-space Jacobian
  - numerical verification
